WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.310
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.580 --> 00:07.980
[Respect Copyright; Everyone's Responsibility]

3
00:08.360 --> 00:09.800
♪Data is screaming♪

4
00:09.800 --> 00:11.330
♪Proposals are burning♪

5
00:11.330 --> 00:13.200
♪I deconstruct the world's algorithms♪

6
00:13.200 --> 00:14.900
♪Only never counting the heartbeat♪

7
00:14.900 --> 00:17.160
♪Whose perfect smile is reflected in the glass?♪

8
00:17.160 --> 00:18.760
♪Treading on shadows as I run ahead♪

9
00:18.760 --> 00:20.300
♪There's no time to fall♪

10
00:20.330 --> 00:23.000
♪They say gears should be obedient♪

11
00:23.100 --> 00:25.660
♪Yet I insist on being the offbeat stopwatch♪

12
00:25.800 --> 00:29.040
♪Planting my own pride in the cracks of the rules♪

13
00:29.200 --> 00:31.800
♪Waiting for the night to grow its dawn♪

14
00:33.200 --> 00:35.930
♪I am my own irreplaceable coordinate♪

15
00:35.930 --> 00:37.280
♪No claimed ground, no comparison♪

16
00:37.280 --> 00:38.660
♪I won't be anyone's footnote♪

17
00:38.660 --> 00:40.040
♪Though there are thousand of templates♪

18
00:40.040 --> 00:41.730
♪I choose only the sharpest second♪

19
00:41.730 --> 00:44.100
♪Answering life as my own thinking question♪

20
00:44.100 --> 00:46.860
♪I am my own never-landing beacon♪

21
00:46.860 --> 00:48.320
♪No borrowed light, no offered prayer♪

22
00:48.320 --> 00:49.530
♪I won't believe in anyone's castle♪

23
00:49.530 --> 00:50.960
♪Even if the world is an exam hall♪

24
00:50.960 --> 00:52.800
♪I'll hand in early and run away♪

25
00:52.800 --> 00:54.100
♪Writing in one single line for the answer♪

26
00:54.460 --> 00:55.820
♪"I dare to claim it!"♪

27
01:05.440 --> 01:07.860
♪I am my own irreplaceable coordinate♪

28
01:07.860 --> 01:09.400
♪No substitute, no imitation♪

29
01:09.400 --> 01:10.560
♪I won't trade for anyone's glory♪

30
01:10.560 --> 01:12.040
♪Though there are thousands of echoes♪

31
01:12.040 --> 01:13.700
♪I listen only to the loneliest second♪

32
01:13.700 --> 01:16.000
♪Walking life into my own exclamation mark♪

33
01:16.000 --> 01:18.760
♪I am my own never-extinguishing lamp♪

34
01:18.760 --> 01:20.360
♪No wind‑borne drift, no shore‑bound rest♪

35
01:20.360 --> 01:21.700
♪I won't linger in anyone's course♪

36
01:21.700 --> 01:23.160
♪Even if there are millions of scripts♪

37
01:23.160 --> 01:24.960
♪I'll tear them up and rewrite today♪

38
01:24.960 --> 01:26.060
♪Signing the signature at the end with only♪

39
01:26.380 --> 01:27.740
♪"I create it!"♪

40
01:33.400 --> 01:37.980
[Irreplaceable]

41
01:37.980 --> 01:40.980
[Episode 19]

42
01:47.980 --> 01:49.860
[Organizational Efficiency Push. Process Efficiency Diagram]

43
01:55.790 --> 01:56.210
Mr. Bu,

44
01:56.790 --> 01:58.020
Tianna's strategic analysis skills

45
01:58.070 --> 01:58.980
are outstanding.

46
02:00.070 --> 02:01.570
If she hadn't left Maxmise,

47
02:02.790 --> 02:04.460
she'd have been the first among us

48
02:04.510 --> 02:05.770
to make partner.

49
02:08.190 --> 02:09.540
With any other entrepreneur,

50
02:09.590 --> 02:11.100
having a successor this good

51
02:12.030 --> 02:13.340
would make them ecstatic.

52
02:15.680 --> 02:16.610
So why haven't you ever

53
02:18.870 --> 02:19.660
put her

54
02:19.710 --> 02:20.850
in a key position?

55
02:22.910 --> 02:23.410
Go on.

56
02:26.400 --> 02:27.130
Tianna blames it all

57
02:27.150 --> 02:28.410
on you favoring boys over girls.

58
02:29.400 --> 02:30.450
I actually think

59
02:32.000 --> 02:32.820
you're afraid.

60
02:35.030 --> 02:36.730
Buffett worked until 90

61
02:36.960 --> 02:37.660
and never handed over power.

62
02:39.000 --> 02:40.010
You're not even 60.

63
02:41.630 --> 02:42.690
I think there's only one reason.

64
02:43.430 --> 02:45.780
You don't want to name a successor too early.

65
02:50.590 --> 02:51.450
The more outstanding

66
02:52.080 --> 02:52.660
Tianna becomes,

67
02:53.520 --> 02:55.100
and the more determined she is to do well at Siwei,

68
02:55.310 --> 02:56.060
the more worried you get.

69
02:56.800 --> 02:58.660
Because she's basically

70
02:59.710 --> 03:00.610
telling you

71
03:01.400 --> 03:02.130
you're getting older.

72
03:03.030 --> 03:04.170
And in a few years,

73
03:06.030 --> 03:08.010
the next generation might replace you.

74
03:08.680 --> 03:09.410
That's why

75
03:10.280 --> 03:12.130
you've always spoiled Tianjie on purpose.

76
03:12.590 --> 03:14.570
You quietly hint to the higher-ups

77
03:14.630 --> 03:16.730
that Tianjie is your successor.

78
03:18.000 --> 03:19.380
Because you know perfectly well

79
03:20.800 --> 03:22.410
that for the next 20 years, until Tianjie is

80
03:22.470 --> 03:23.690
the same age Tianna is now,

81
03:24.840 --> 03:26.100
you need to keep

82
03:27.590 --> 03:29.850
Siwei's power firmly in your own hands.

83
03:36.080 --> 03:36.500
Mr. Bu,

84
03:37.680 --> 03:38.780
if you want the business to last,

85
03:39.960 --> 03:42.010
you have to focus on building a management pipeline.

86
03:43.000 --> 03:43.690
Tianna has

87
03:43.750 --> 03:44.730
zero sense of security.

88
03:45.960 --> 03:48.820
All her arrogance and anger

89
03:50.470 --> 03:51.570
really come down to one thing.

90
03:54.310 --> 03:55.060
She's scared

91
03:56.750 --> 03:58.290
that one day you'll stop loving her.

92
03:59.400 --> 04:00.130
Or

93
04:01.840 --> 04:03.380
she's scared of being replaced

94
04:03.870 --> 04:04.540
by her brother.

95
04:08.630 --> 04:09.380
You love Tianna

96
04:10.280 --> 04:11.890
more than I ever could.

97
04:12.630 --> 04:13.410
But no matter what,

98
04:13.470 --> 04:14.660
I still need to remind you,

99
04:15.800 --> 04:17.020
the heart is flesh,

100
04:17.480 --> 04:17.930
not steel.

101
04:18.750 --> 04:19.780
You can forge and temper steel,

102
04:21.360 --> 04:22.930
but once a heart breaks,

103
04:24.800 --> 04:25.810
it never heals.

104
04:32.000 --> 04:32.730
That hurts.

105
04:32.870 --> 04:33.580
Are you okay,

106
04:33.920 --> 04:34.340
Jie?

107
04:34.920 --> 04:36.340
I'm fine.

108
04:36.510 --> 04:38.460
If he doesn't like it, don't force him.

109
04:38.630 --> 04:39.900
Who's forcing him?

110
04:40.480 --> 04:41.660
He insists on practicing.

111
04:42.040 --> 04:43.580
The more it hurts, the more he goes at it.

112
04:45.510 --> 04:46.050
Jie,

113
04:46.830 --> 04:47.810
do you really like it that much?

114
04:48.870 --> 04:49.900
When I grow up,

115
04:50.240 --> 04:51.140
I wanna compete,

116
04:51.480 --> 04:53.370
make the Olympics, and win glory for the country.

117
04:54.480 --> 04:54.930
Jie,

118
04:55.390 --> 04:55.980
don't talk nonsense.

119
04:56.310 --> 04:57.490
You need to study hard.

120
04:57.920 --> 04:59.660
That way, when you're older, you can be Dad's right-hand man.

121
05:00.240 --> 05:01.730
I don't wanna be busy

122
05:01.800 --> 05:02.730
like Tianna.

123
05:02.870 --> 05:04.050
Studying's exhausting.

124
05:04.360 --> 05:05.140
I just wanna play.

125
05:06.630 --> 05:07.220
Watch out!

126
05:07.430 --> 05:08.100
Move, you two.

127
05:14.000 --> 05:15.020
Didn't you say their school

128
05:15.070 --> 05:16.810
did a potential model test on him?

129
05:17.190 --> 05:17.730
Let me see.

130
05:18.870 --> 05:19.930
He's still little.

131
05:19.950 --> 05:20.780
It doesn't count.

132
05:21.360 --> 05:22.540
Just let me see.

133
05:26.160 --> 05:26.540
This...

134
05:26.800 --> 05:27.170
Not really...

135
05:30.680 --> 05:31.490
What's this?

136
05:31.950 --> 05:33.250
Linguistic aptitude, logical aptitude,

137
05:33.310 --> 05:34.460
and management skills are all average.

138
05:35.240 --> 05:35.700
But

139
05:36.120 --> 05:38.140
spatial ability and athletic ability are outstanding.

140
05:45.190 --> 05:46.170
Do you really think

141
05:46.600 --> 05:47.810
Tianjie is more suited

142
05:48.000 --> 05:49.730
to take over Siwei Group than Tianna?

143
05:50.160 --> 05:51.810
If those two ever turn on each other,

144
05:53.040 --> 05:53.850
can you really

145
05:57.630 --> 05:58.930
live out your later years happily?

146
06:14.270 --> 06:15.410
There's a full team meeting tomorrow morning.

147
06:15.720 --> 06:16.700
We'll go over the project proposal.

148
06:16.800 --> 06:17.730
Is 10:30 okay for you?

149
06:18.750 --> 06:19.170
Chi?

150
06:21.600 --> 06:22.140
Chi?

151
06:25.270 --> 06:26.780
I zoned out. What were you saying?

152
06:30.720 --> 06:31.290
What's wrong?

153
06:32.510 --> 06:33.290
Are you just too tired?

154
06:34.190 --> 06:34.930
No.

155
06:36.750 --> 06:38.410
Tianna and Zhao Heng are going through a breakup.

156
06:38.870 --> 06:40.610
Zhao Heng's about to go on a long business trip to South America.

157
06:40.680 --> 06:41.610
I'm a little worried about them.

158
06:44.600 --> 06:45.610
From my experience,

159
06:46.000 --> 06:47.100
even with your best friends,

160
06:47.510 --> 06:48.610
when it comes to stuff like this,

161
06:48.830 --> 06:50.100
it's best to just listen.

162
06:51.630 --> 06:53.140
Whatever you do, don't give a strong opinion.

163
06:53.600 --> 06:54.460
Otherwise, whether they

164
06:54.630 --> 06:55.220
get back together

165
06:55.270 --> 06:56.140
or break up later,

166
06:56.950 --> 06:57.900
you'll be stuck in the middle

167
06:58.000 --> 06:58.700
and get on both their bad sides.

168
06:59.120 --> 07:00.540
But I don't wanna do that.

169
07:01.270 --> 07:02.850
That safe, cautious approach

170
07:02.920 --> 07:04.020
feels outdated to me.

171
07:04.310 --> 07:04.730
Look,

172
07:05.000 --> 07:06.490
clients pick a consulting firm

173
07:06.560 --> 07:07.730
because they want a clear stance

174
07:07.800 --> 07:08.700
and a definitive opinion.

175
07:09.160 --> 07:09.930
So as a friend,

176
07:10.000 --> 07:11.660
if I'm all wishy-washy right now,

177
07:12.600 --> 07:14.050
I feel like a bad friend.

178
07:16.270 --> 07:18.170
Even if I get on both their bad sides,

179
07:18.430 --> 07:19.490
that's a problem for later, right?

180
07:20.600 --> 07:21.730
But now it's killing me to just sit here

181
07:21.830 --> 07:22.460
and do nothing.

182
07:27.310 --> 07:28.020
I'm gonna go make a call.

183
07:28.070 --> 07:29.250
Give me ten minutes, and I'll be back to work.

184
07:46.120 --> 07:47.560
[Xu Chi]

185
07:55.950 --> 07:56.290
Hello?

186
07:56.600 --> 07:57.290
Are you at the airport?

187
07:57.920 --> 07:58.900
You know that too?

188
07:59.920 --> 08:00.610
You want me to bring you back

189
08:00.680 --> 08:01.540
souvenirs from South America?

190
08:02.000 --> 08:02.780
Be honest with me,

191
08:03.240 --> 08:04.170
when you picked up my call,

192
08:04.190 --> 08:05.170
were you really disappointed?

193
08:05.630 --> 08:06.730
You were hoping

194
08:06.750 --> 08:07.850
it was Tianna calling, right?

195
08:10.510 --> 08:12.170
She won't. With that temper of hers...

196
08:12.240 --> 08:13.250
Zhao Heng, listen to me.

197
08:13.680 --> 08:14.850
We all want equality

198
08:14.920 --> 08:15.730
in love.

199
08:15.800 --> 08:17.170
We all want to be evenly matched.

200
08:18.160 --> 08:18.900
But let me ask you,

201
08:19.950 --> 08:21.540
are you actually on equal footing with Tianna?

202
08:22.240 --> 08:23.410
You know her weak spot

203
08:23.480 --> 08:24.490
is that she never felt secure

204
08:24.600 --> 08:25.370
in her own family.

205
08:25.680 --> 08:26.100
And yet

206
08:26.750 --> 08:27.580
you went and did

207
08:27.600 --> 08:28.700
the one thing she hates most,

208
08:28.750 --> 08:30.370
and then expected her to treat you rationally.

209
08:30.950 --> 08:32.100
Tianna was with me

210
08:32.150 --> 08:32.980
before she came to find you.

211
08:33.550 --> 08:34.530
She thought

212
08:34.600 --> 08:35.460
her dad was riding you hard again,

213
08:35.510 --> 08:36.100
and she panicked.

214
08:36.480 --> 08:37.370
She almost twisted her ankle

215
08:37.440 --> 08:38.340
running to the parking lot.

216
08:38.390 --> 08:39.220
Did you know that?

217
08:40.240 --> 08:41.370
You said you lost the bet.

218
08:42.360 --> 08:43.770
Zhao Heng, is it really all or nothing for you

219
08:43.840 --> 08:44.820
when it comes to love?

220
08:45.270 --> 08:46.130
I know

221
08:46.600 --> 08:48.250
it's totally biased of me

222
08:48.670 --> 08:49.180
to come at you

223
08:49.270 --> 08:50.650
for taking Tianna's side right now.

224
08:52.600 --> 08:53.530
But as a friend,

225
08:53.600 --> 08:54.850
I really don't want you to regret this.

226
08:56.910 --> 08:57.850
In two months,

227
08:59.390 --> 09:00.610
love can snap

228
09:00.670 --> 09:01.220
like a thread.

229
09:01.750 --> 09:03.060
Even if you want to tie it back together,

230
09:04.270 --> 09:05.340
at ten thousand kilometers apart,

231
09:07.480 --> 09:08.300
can you even reach it?

232
09:20.180 --> 09:21.300
Oh, man.

233
09:21.960 --> 09:23.180
I pushed too hard on the toilet.

234
09:23.510 --> 09:24.100
Feeling a little dizzy.

235
09:25.750 --> 09:26.530
Doesn't your watch check

236
09:26.550 --> 09:27.180
blood pressure?

237
09:27.270 --> 09:27.940
Let me borrow it.

238
09:32.750 --> 09:33.220
Where's your watch?

239
09:33.870 --> 09:34.300
You lost it?

240
09:35.270 --> 09:35.580
Hold on.

241
09:35.630 --> 09:36.460
Let me track it on my phone.

242
09:37.960 --> 09:38.440
[Zhao Heng's Smartwatch]

243
09:38.510 --> 09:40.420
Parking lot P1?

244
09:42.390 --> 09:42.850
That's not right.

245
09:44.000 --> 09:45.300
We took a ride

246
09:45.390 --> 09:46.490
straight to the departures level.

247
09:47.120 --> 09:48.530
How's your watch in here?

248
09:50.720 --> 09:51.940
Maybe you left the watch in the car,

249
09:51.960 --> 09:53.980
and the driver went to P1 to wait for passengers?

250
09:55.360 --> 09:56.250
You're dead set

251
09:56.270 --> 09:57.250
on mooching off me.

252
09:57.790 --> 09:58.730
You're in no position to talk about equality.

253
09:58.790 --> 09:59.420
Bu Tianna!

254
10:05.320 --> 10:05.940
Where are you going?

255
10:05.980 --> 10:06.490
We're about to board!

256
10:59.740 --> 11:00.250
Tianna.

257
11:35.380 --> 11:36.490
When I said I wanted to break up,

258
11:38.030 --> 11:39.180
I was just acting out.

259
11:39.870 --> 11:40.850
I was gaslighting you.

260
11:42.020 --> 11:43.180
I wanted to make sure you couldn't leave me.

261
11:50.030 --> 11:50.980
But deep down, I know

262
11:54.030 --> 11:55.700
no one could ever replace you in my heart.

263
11:58.910 --> 11:59.580
So,

264
12:01.600 --> 12:02.460
will you forgive me?

265
12:08.240 --> 12:09.370
I'm not here for you.

266
12:10.030 --> 12:10.460
Right.

267
12:11.510 --> 12:12.370
You're just passing by.

268
12:13.360 --> 12:14.340
I'm the one who came for you.

269
12:17.600 --> 12:18.530
You scumbag.

270
12:19.360 --> 12:21.010
Why do you always tell me what sounds good?

271
12:22.910 --> 12:23.220
Yeah.

272
12:23.910 --> 12:24.490
I'm a scumbag.

273
12:25.440 --> 12:25.890
I'm awful.

274
12:26.510 --> 12:27.010
I'm trash.

275
12:27.870 --> 12:29.100
I had an ulterior motive this whole time.

276
12:30.080 --> 12:30.580
So,

277
12:34.030 --> 12:34.770
do you still love me?

278
13:17.510 --> 13:18.180
And then?

279
13:18.480 --> 13:19.220
What happened next?

280
13:20.120 --> 13:20.650
And then

281
13:21.150 --> 13:22.130
his colleague called

282
13:22.240 --> 13:23.180
and told Zhao Heng to board.

283
13:23.360 --> 13:24.490
Then he and Tianna agreed to

284
13:24.510 --> 13:25.650
video chat

285
13:25.720 --> 13:26.650
for at least half an hour every day.

286
13:26.720 --> 13:27.730
After that, Zhao Heng flew off.

287
13:29.440 --> 13:30.100
That's it?

288
13:31.440 --> 13:33.220
That's so not romantic.

289
13:33.600 --> 13:34.580
I figured Zhao Heng

290
13:34.630 --> 13:35.580
would've at least changed his ticket

291
13:35.630 --> 13:36.530
and stayed one more night.

292
13:37.120 --> 13:38.010
Or Bu Tianna

293
13:38.080 --> 13:38.650
would've bought a ticket

294
13:38.790 --> 13:40.060
and gone to Venezuela with him.

295
13:41.200 --> 13:41.730
Mr. Shen,

296
13:41.840 --> 13:43.530
you think this is some idol drama?

297
13:44.360 --> 13:45.300
Feelings matter, of course.

298
13:45.360 --> 13:46.460
But that's just between two people.

299
13:46.510 --> 13:47.130
Work

300
13:47.150 --> 13:48.220
involves the whole team.

301
13:48.270 --> 13:49.300
You've gotta make trade-offs.

302
13:50.910 --> 13:51.730
So,

303
13:51.790 --> 13:53.580
to you, consulting people,

304
13:54.030 --> 13:55.850
work always comes before love, huh?

305
13:57.240 --> 13:57.850
First,

306
13:57.910 --> 13:59.650
I partly agree with you.

307
13:59.750 --> 14:00.420
Second,

308
14:00.960 --> 14:02.220
I think I hear

309
14:02.270 --> 14:03.340
a little bitterness in there.

310
14:04.270 --> 14:05.010
Third,

311
14:05.320 --> 14:06.700
my boss

312
14:06.960 --> 14:07.890
is blowing up my phone.

313
14:08.000 --> 14:08.730
So I'm gonna head out.

314
14:08.840 --> 14:09.650
I'll leave you two to your date.

315
14:15.790 --> 14:17.250
Something's off.

316
14:19.440 --> 14:21.010
That girl's definitely got something going on.

317
14:21.960 --> 14:23.130
But she really is thoughtful.

318
14:24.440 --> 14:24.770
Oh,

319
14:25.030 --> 14:25.530
try this.

320
14:26.120 --> 14:26.610
Foie gras.

321
14:28.120 --> 14:28.980
It's a bit rich,

322
14:29.480 --> 14:30.820
but it's loaded with iron.

323
14:31.240 --> 14:31.940
Good for your blood.

324
14:32.080 --> 14:32.580
Try it.

325
14:34.240 --> 14:34.770
Good?

326
14:35.750 --> 14:36.460
Have some more.

327
14:38.670 --> 14:39.580
I wish you could take

328
14:39.600 --> 14:40.850
a vacation sometime.

329
14:41.080 --> 14:42.220
Then we'll go somewhere for a couple of days.

330
14:42.840 --> 14:43.700
We can find a nice

331
14:43.720 --> 14:44.610
lake or ocean

332
14:44.720 --> 14:45.700
and just relax.

333
14:46.510 --> 14:47.890
Lately, I've even dreamed

334
14:47.960 --> 14:48.770
about you kayaking with me.

335
14:48.840 --> 14:49.770
I was so happy.

336
14:50.200 --> 14:50.940
Then let's do this Saturday.

337
14:51.840 --> 14:52.180
No,

338
14:52.390 --> 14:52.890
if you don't...

339
14:55.750 --> 14:56.530
What, you don't want to?

340
14:58.790 --> 15:00.010
I'd love to.

341
15:00.750 --> 15:01.250
Really?

342
15:02.790 --> 15:03.100
Alright.

343
15:03.870 --> 15:04.580
I'll go find

344
15:04.600 --> 15:05.130
a romantic hotel

345
15:05.630 --> 15:06.580
tonight.

346
15:06.910 --> 15:08.060
Let's have ourselves a nice romantic time.

347
15:10.440 --> 15:11.180
Have some meat.

348
15:11.270 --> 15:11.980
I haven't finished this piece yet.

349
15:12.030 --> 15:12.370
You go ahead.

350
15:21.150 --> 15:21.700
What's wrong?

351
15:21.750 --> 15:22.890
Didn't sleep well last night?

352
15:23.870 --> 15:24.250
It was okay.

353
15:25.030 --> 15:25.340
By the way,

354
15:25.390 --> 15:26.340
tomorrow morning's meeting...

355
15:26.910 --> 15:28.180
I already coordinated with everyone else.

356
15:28.270 --> 15:29.700
10:30, meeting room A2.

357
15:31.030 --> 15:32.220
So how's the All Buy timeline

358
15:32.270 --> 15:32.940
coming along?

359
15:33.630 --> 15:34.610
I coordinated with Lele

360
15:34.670 --> 15:35.820
and got All Buy's side set up.

361
15:36.200 --> 15:37.700
Starting next Monday,

362
15:37.790 --> 15:39.010
it'll be Warehousing first,

363
15:39.080 --> 15:40.130
followed by Quality Assurance,

364
15:40.270 --> 15:41.940
and then R&D and Procurement middle office.

365
15:42.080 --> 15:42.770
The whole process

366
15:42.790 --> 15:43.940
should take about half a month.

367
15:44.480 --> 15:45.890
Then we can start

368
15:46.120 --> 15:47.370
updating and iterating the model.

369
15:47.840 --> 15:48.580
Nice.

370
15:48.790 --> 15:50.060
That's fast progress.

371
15:50.790 --> 15:51.490
Looks like

372
15:51.750 --> 15:52.940
things are fine on Bu Tianna's end?

373
15:54.720 --> 15:55.580
You guessed right.

374
15:56.240 --> 15:57.530
Good thing I didn't listen to you that day.

375
16:00.630 --> 16:01.300
Sorry.

376
16:02.600 --> 16:03.580
I guess

377
16:03.960 --> 16:05.100
I'm a bit old-school.

378
16:06.080 --> 16:06.420
Wait,

379
16:06.440 --> 16:07.650
why're you apologizing?

380
16:08.000 --> 16:09.100
I didn't mean it that way.

381
16:10.270 --> 16:11.340
I know you were just

382
16:11.440 --> 16:12.460
giving me

383
16:12.550 --> 16:13.180
a mature suggestion

384
16:13.390 --> 16:14.580
from where you stand.

385
16:15.150 --> 16:15.650
You mean it?

386
16:16.910 --> 16:17.580
Yes.

387
16:21.480 --> 16:22.250
What... what's wrong?

388
16:30.240 --> 16:31.460
I'm handing you my whole heart.

389
16:31.510 --> 16:32.060
Hear that?

390
16:34.550 --> 16:35.100
Is it real?

391
16:36.600 --> 16:37.340
So real.

392
16:38.720 --> 16:39.370
I'm so moved.

393
16:41.120 --> 16:42.180
You're putting it on.

394
16:42.180 --> 16:46.460
♪Orange sky at dusk; the evening breeze is waiting♪

395
16:46.580 --> 16:51.620
♪The crowd at the crossing suddenly scatters♪

396
16:51.700 --> 17:00.140
♪This world moves too fast, yet you walk slowly toward me♪

397
17:02.020 --> 17:06.820
♪We're like the evening breeze tangling with the clouds♪

398
17:07.780 --> 17:11.060
♪Strolling among the clouds, waiting for the sky to clear♪

399
17:11.070 --> 17:11.920
[Testing]

400
17:12.340 --> 17:16.660
♪Last time you had something left unsaid, right?♪

401
17:16.790 --> 17:17.180
Mr. Liu,

402
17:17.440 --> 17:17.860
thank you.

403
17:18.200 --> 17:18.770
No worries.

404
17:19.510 --> 17:20.010
Mr. Ye,

405
17:20.550 --> 17:22.460
after you guys optimize this process,

406
17:22.680 --> 17:23.660
will there be any side effects?

407
17:24.350 --> 17:25.090
Don't worry.

408
17:25.400 --> 17:26.330
It'll only boost efficiency.

409
17:26.590 --> 17:27.730
Won't cause any trouble.

410
17:28.550 --> 17:28.940
Alright.

411
17:28.940 --> 17:32.540
♪Through the muddy fields, rushing toward the sea♪

412
17:32.660 --> 17:37.620
♪I know you'll be waiting there♪

413
17:37.740 --> 17:38.860
♪Together with me♪

414
17:38.880 --> 17:39.810
Based on the AI model

415
17:39.880 --> 17:40.860
we developed at Hezong,

416
17:41.000 --> 17:42.140
[All Buy] when All Buy goes overseas,

417
17:42.200 --> 17:42.860
they should focus

418
17:42.960 --> 17:44.660
on packaged foods,

419
17:44.750 --> 17:45.460
mainly snack foods

420
17:45.480 --> 17:46.810
and instant grains and oils.

421
17:47.110 --> 17:47.940
For where to land,

422
17:48.000 --> 17:49.620
I'd suggest major cities with dense Chinese

423
17:49.680 --> 17:50.730
and international student populations,

424
17:51.110 --> 17:52.050
because these products

425
17:52.110 --> 17:53.570
keep well and are easy to ship.

426
17:53.680 --> 17:54.980
Plus, we can use AI for both quality inspection

427
17:55.110 --> 17:56.090
and quality assurance.

428
17:56.200 --> 17:57.140
That can massively boost efficiency

429
17:57.440 --> 17:58.290
and cut the labor costs

430
17:58.350 --> 17:59.180
of setting up overseas

431
17:59.240 --> 17:59.900
quality control centers.

432
18:01.790 --> 18:02.420
Put together

433
18:02.440 --> 18:03.860
the overseas e-commerce proposal

434
18:03.880 --> 18:04.420
for All Buy.

435
18:04.640 --> 18:05.290
Okay, got it.

436
18:06.110 --> 18:06.660
And take a look at this.

437
18:08.350 --> 18:09.660
Let's go over this.

438
18:10.830 --> 18:11.660
I was gonna bring it up too.

439
18:11.720 --> 18:12.530
Just help me

440
18:12.550 --> 18:13.220
adjust all of these.

441
18:13.510 --> 18:13.810
Okay?

442
18:14.110 --> 18:14.900
Everyone's tired, right?

443
18:15.070 --> 18:16.140
I bought coffee and milk tea

444
18:16.160 --> 18:16.810
for everyone.

445
18:16.960 --> 18:17.860
Take a break.

446
18:18.240 --> 18:19.770
- Thanks, Mr. Kai. - Thanks, Mr. Kai.

447
18:23.160 --> 18:24.290
Made this especially for you.

448
18:24.510 --> 18:26.050
Your favorite.

449
18:27.240 --> 18:28.570
Triple espresso with whiskey.

450
18:28.590 --> 18:29.980
Hand-poured Irish. Did I remember right?

451
18:30.830 --> 18:31.290
Thanks.

452
18:31.790 --> 18:32.090
Sit.

453
18:33.680 --> 18:34.900
So, how much longer

454
18:35.310 --> 18:36.810
till we see the light at the end of the tunnel?

455
18:37.310 --> 18:37.660
Soon.

456
18:38.590 --> 18:39.290
All Buy's feedback

457
18:39.350 --> 18:40.090
has been pretty good.

458
18:40.270 --> 18:41.290
They got inspired by us

459
18:41.640 --> 18:42.700
and plan to use the AI vendor

460
18:42.720 --> 18:43.490
we recommended

461
18:43.640 --> 18:44.980
to overhaul their

462
18:45.030 --> 18:46.140
domestic backend,

463
18:46.200 --> 18:47.460
both warehousing and outlets.

464
18:47.790 --> 18:49.490
I figure two weeks at most,

465
18:50.310 --> 18:51.330
and we can do the official delivery.

466
18:52.720 --> 18:54.770
We do their overseas consulting,

467
18:54.830 --> 18:56.660
and they just port it over domestically.

468
18:57.270 --> 18:58.770
They're getting a steal.

469
18:58.920 --> 18:59.940
One consulting fee; double the usage.

470
19:00.160 --> 19:00.980
No choice.

471
19:01.550 --> 19:03.330
Just treat it as free advertising.

472
19:03.550 --> 19:05.700
All Buy is practically a stepping stone

473
19:05.790 --> 19:07.660
for Hezong to break into the tech giant ecosystem.

474
19:08.110 --> 19:08.530
Anyway,

475
19:08.590 --> 19:09.660
as long as this delivery succeeds,

476
19:10.000 --> 19:10.980
we won't have to worry about future deals.

477
19:11.070 --> 19:12.490
Okay, I'm waiting for your victory news.

478
19:14.510 --> 19:14.980
By the way, Mr. Kai...

479
19:16.880 --> 19:18.220
After this project wraps,

480
19:19.440 --> 19:20.770
I want to take a month-long vacation.

481
19:32.440 --> 19:33.010
No problem.

482
19:42.000 --> 19:43.770
A month? Seriously?

483
19:44.160 --> 19:44.530
Yeah.

484
19:44.880 --> 19:46.140
I already gave Mr. Kai a heads-up.

485
19:47.030 --> 19:47.570
Just so HR can easily

486
19:47.590 --> 19:48.530
sign off on your time off.

487
19:49.030 --> 19:50.090
That's great!

488
19:50.830 --> 19:51.770
When I said

489
19:51.790 --> 19:52.860
I had no time to hang out,

490
19:53.000 --> 19:54.180
you looked so down,

491
19:54.240 --> 19:55.220
like a sad golden retriever.

492
19:55.510 --> 19:56.700
It actually made me feel kinda bad.

493
19:57.480 --> 19:57.980
Great.

494
19:58.000 --> 19:58.810
Finally, we get some time

495
19:58.830 --> 19:59.620
just for us.

496
20:00.400 --> 20:00.700
By the way,

497
20:02.110 --> 20:02.730
where do you wanna go?

498
20:04.110 --> 20:04.810
Let me think.

499
20:08.680 --> 20:10.900
Southeast Asia's too close.

500
20:11.920 --> 20:13.090
South America's far.

501
20:13.200 --> 20:14.250
But Tianna and Zhao Heng said

502
20:14.270 --> 20:15.530
they couldn't get used to the food there.

503
20:18.240 --> 20:19.380
How about Saudi Arabia?

504
20:20.240 --> 20:21.010
When I was little,

505
20:21.070 --> 20:22.010
I loved this comic

506
20:22.070 --> 20:23.090
my mom left me.

507
20:23.510 --> 20:24.900
There was a tower that reached for the heavens.

508
20:25.510 --> 20:26.420
My mom said

509
20:26.480 --> 20:28.420
date palms grew in a row at the bottom.

510
20:28.880 --> 20:30.180
The dates were sweet as honey.

511
20:30.350 --> 20:31.250
She loved eating them.

512
20:34.640 --> 20:36.730
The yellow spiral tower?

513
20:36.790 --> 20:37.380
Yes, that one.

514
20:39.030 --> 20:39.860
That's in Iraq,

515
20:39.960 --> 20:40.620
not Saudi.

516
20:45.990 --> 20:47.300
We'd have to take so many days off, though.

517
20:47.560 --> 20:48.770
Chi, if you wanna go,

518
20:49.150 --> 20:50.330
we can take as many days off as we need.

519
20:54.590 --> 20:55.410
Forget it, forget it.

520
20:56.200 --> 20:57.460
Even if we can get the time off,

521
20:58.040 --> 20:59.500
getting there would be a hassle.

522
21:01.400 --> 21:02.050
Where do you wanna go?

523
21:02.880 --> 21:03.620
I love the ocean.

524
21:04.310 --> 21:06.810
I wanna go to the Blue Hole in Dahab.

525
21:07.550 --> 21:09.010
They also call it the Eye of the Ocean.

526
21:09.680 --> 21:11.140
It's the easiest deep blue sea cave

527
21:11.590 --> 21:12.940
for tourists to get to.

528
21:13.310 --> 21:14.420
Then let's go there.

529
21:15.590 --> 21:16.900
We've got a whole month.

530
21:17.350 --> 21:18.570
We can hit the Tower of Babel first,

531
21:18.720 --> 21:19.660
then the Blue Hole.

532
21:20.160 --> 21:20.860
They say

533
21:20.920 --> 21:22.420
that the Tower of Babel is where humans

534
21:22.550 --> 21:23.660
get closest to the heavens.

535
21:24.070 --> 21:24.810
We could go from

536
21:25.000 --> 21:26.940
the highest point on Earth

537
21:27.480 --> 21:28.770
straight to the deepest.

538
21:31.270 --> 21:32.290
How do you

539
21:32.310 --> 21:33.860
make everything

540
21:34.160 --> 21:35.810
sound so poetic?

541
21:40.960 --> 21:42.250
Must be that mature man charm

542
21:43.200 --> 21:44.180
you talked about.

543
21:48.240 --> 21:49.380
You're so petty,

544
21:50.000 --> 21:51.380
and you hold grudges.

545
21:52.030 --> 21:52.570
Yeah.

546
21:53.240 --> 21:53.860
I hold grudges.

547
21:54.830 --> 21:55.700
And right now,

548
21:56.000 --> 21:56.900
I'm getting revenge.

549
21:57.270 --> 21:57.980
Here I come!

550
21:59.480 --> 22:01.330
What are you doing? We have to get up early tomorrow.

551
22:27.830 --> 22:31.050
Go from the highest point on Earth...

552
22:43.350 --> 22:45.330
We could go from

553
22:48.030 --> 22:50.900
the highest point on Earth...

554
22:56.750 --> 22:57.860
[I'm in Beijing] It's that supervisor surnamed Liu

555
22:57.920 --> 22:58.810
from All Buy's quality inspection department.

556
22:59.400 --> 23:00.180
Before it happened,

557
23:00.200 --> 23:01.090
he posted a farewell video

558
23:01.110 --> 23:02.050
on a video app.

559
23:02.510 --> 23:03.810
Said All Buy and Hezong teamed up

560
23:03.880 --> 23:04.660
to force him out.

561
23:05.680 --> 23:07.220
That consultant Ye

562
23:08.200 --> 23:10.090
swore up and down

563
23:10.440 --> 23:11.460
that after optimizing the process,

564
23:11.830 --> 23:13.940
[Statement] it wouldn't cause us any trouble.

565
23:14.680 --> 23:16.250
What a liar.

566
23:18.750 --> 23:20.770
We're exactly the trouble

567
23:20.830 --> 23:23.660
All Buy wants to cut loose!

568
23:28.880 --> 23:30.010
Word is, Mr. Liu

569
23:30.070 --> 23:31.530
has over three million in mortgage debt.

570
23:31.640 --> 23:32.660
His kid's still in the hospital.

571
23:32.920 --> 23:34.380
That AI quality inspection system

572
23:34.480 --> 23:35.900
All Buy brought in

573
23:36.160 --> 23:37.460
uses robotic electronic eyes

574
23:37.550 --> 23:38.380
and probes

575
23:38.440 --> 23:39.420
to replace human inspectors.

576
23:39.790 --> 23:41.180
One machine can replace

577
23:41.270 --> 23:42.330
fifty quality inspectors.

578
23:42.590 --> 23:43.380
[Hotspot Intel] So listen up, folks,

579
23:43.680 --> 23:44.140
AI

580
23:44.160 --> 23:45.250
doesn't just revolutionize industries.

581
23:45.510 --> 23:46.620
It can cost lives.

582
23:46.790 --> 23:48.290
- Mr. Su. - Mr. Su!

583
23:48.310 --> 23:49.290
Is what Mr. Liu said

584
23:49.310 --> 23:50.250
in his video true?

585
23:50.680 --> 23:51.860
Did your company spend a fortune

586
23:51.920 --> 23:52.770
hiring consultants to lay people off,

587
23:52.790 --> 23:53.570
instead of giving old employees

588
23:53.590 --> 23:54.180
fair compensation?

589
23:54.480 --> 23:55.010
Please answer directly.

590
23:55.070 --> 23:55.490
Mr. Su.

591
23:55.720 --> 23:56.660
Please answer directly.

592
23:56.680 --> 23:56.940
Mr. Su.

593
23:57.200 --> 23:58.420
Mr. Su. Did someone die at your company?

594
23:58.680 --> 23:59.290
Did someone jump?

595
24:09.440 --> 24:10.220
Are you sure HR

596
24:10.240 --> 24:11.140
never pressured him to resign?

597
24:11.480 --> 24:11.860
Yes.

598
24:12.240 --> 24:13.810
That's not what you told us back then.

599
24:13.920 --> 24:14.700
This all happened so suddenly.

600
24:14.750 --> 24:15.700
Fine. I'll talk to Mr. Ye.

601
24:16.750 --> 24:17.460
I understand.

602
24:20.000 --> 24:20.620
There you are.

603
24:21.960 --> 24:22.700
The hospital said

604
24:22.830 --> 24:23.330
Mr. Liu

605
24:23.350 --> 24:24.090
is out of the ICU.

606
24:24.480 --> 24:26.140
He hit a light sign on the 29th floor,

607
24:26.200 --> 24:27.290
then landed on a platform on the 7th.

608
24:27.350 --> 24:28.250
He's not in any danger.

609
24:29.440 --> 24:29.940
Thank god.

610
24:30.680 --> 24:31.490
I'm going to see him right now.

611
24:32.310 --> 24:32.900
I'll come with you.

612
24:35.030 --> 24:35.490
Xu Chi!

613
24:36.350 --> 24:37.530
All Buy's on the line for you.

614
24:39.590 --> 24:40.860
You go ahead. I'll catch up.

615
24:43.110 --> 24:43.730
Richard!

616
24:46.750 --> 24:47.620
Are you going to the hospital?

617
24:50.480 --> 24:51.810
The crisis PR team is already there.

618
24:51.880 --> 24:52.660
You don't need to go.

619
24:54.680 --> 24:55.330
Mr. Kai,

620
24:57.030 --> 24:57.860
I want to apologize

621
24:58.830 --> 24:59.620
to Mr. Liu in person.

622
25:00.960 --> 25:02.730
We've always handled overseas projects.

623
25:02.790 --> 25:04.660
Domestic projects have always been yours.

624
25:04.830 --> 25:06.050
We can't take this one.

625
25:10.200 --> 25:11.460
You're back already?

626
25:14.920 --> 25:15.660
Mr. Kai said

627
25:16.310 --> 25:17.250
I'm not ready to go yet.

628
25:18.240 --> 25:19.380
I get how that video

629
25:19.440 --> 25:20.250
affected you.

630
25:20.830 --> 25:21.530
But

631
25:21.640 --> 25:22.980
you need to control your guilt.

632
25:23.510 --> 25:25.220
Mr. Liu didn't mention your name.

633
25:25.510 --> 25:26.530
If you go apologize now,

634
25:26.590 --> 25:28.220
you're taking all the blame

635
25:28.270 --> 25:29.460
on yourself.

636
25:29.750 --> 25:30.940
He just got stuck

637
25:31.240 --> 25:32.490
in his own head for a moment.

638
25:32.590 --> 25:34.050
He's fine now.

639
25:36.350 --> 25:36.860
Mr. Kai,

640
25:38.350 --> 25:39.330
that's a human life.

641
25:39.640 --> 25:40.050
Okay.

642
25:41.160 --> 25:42.490
I get how you feel.

643
25:43.240 --> 25:44.050
It's like, I didn't kill him,

644
25:44.070 --> 25:45.090
but he died because of me.

645
25:45.350 --> 25:47.180
But how we handle this case now

646
25:48.270 --> 25:49.700
isn't just about Mr. Liu.

647
25:49.830 --> 25:51.250
It's about billions in business,

648
25:51.480 --> 25:54.010
and new jobs for hundreds of employees.

649
25:55.110 --> 25:56.290
Don't lose sight of the big picture.

650
25:58.480 --> 25:58.980
Mr. Kai.

651
26:00.480 --> 26:01.460
I'm a partner.

652
26:02.350 --> 26:03.140
This is my project.

653
26:04.310 --> 26:05.620
I get first say over this!

654
26:09.160 --> 26:10.570
There are a lot of reporters outside the hospital.

655
26:10.750 --> 26:11.900
If you go now, you could cause

656
26:11.920 --> 26:12.770
irreversible second-hand harm

657
26:12.830 --> 26:13.980
to Mr. Liu and his family.

658
26:14.070 --> 26:15.420
Have you thought about that?

659
26:16.720 --> 26:17.730
Setting aside that I'm your boss,

660
26:18.240 --> 26:19.220
as a friend,

661
26:19.270 --> 26:21.140
I'm suggesting you go home and rest.

662
26:21.440 --> 26:23.140
Wait till you're in a better place

663
26:23.240 --> 26:24.980
and PR has things under control.

664
26:25.070 --> 26:26.250
It won't be too late then.

665
26:26.550 --> 26:27.220
But Mr. Kai...

666
26:27.270 --> 26:27.860
Enough!

667
26:28.400 --> 26:29.290
Richard, I've got a lot of fires

668
26:29.310 --> 26:30.090
to put out right now.

669
26:30.310 --> 26:31.490
Can you just give it a rest?

670
26:33.240 --> 26:33.860
Chi,

671
26:34.750 --> 26:36.570
actually, back when we were on the Yuanzhou project,

672
26:37.400 --> 26:38.570
I started thinking about something.

673
26:40.160 --> 26:41.330
We in consulting

674
26:42.640 --> 26:44.460
shouldn't just be responsible to the companies we serve.

675
